.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring-context 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-context \- Names, lists and selects contexts, so commands need no flags
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring context\fR [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Names, lists and selects contexts, so commands need no flags
.PP
A context names a fleet\*(Aqs control addresses, certificates and principal (ADR\-0043).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fleetring\-context\-list(1)
Lists the contexts, marking the current one
.TP
fleetring\-context\-show(1)
Shows one context: the current one unless a name is given
.TP
fleetring\-context\-current(1)
Prints the current context\*(Aqs name and nothing else, for a shell prompt
.TP
fleetring\-context\-add(1)
Adds a context: a name for a fleet\*(Aqs control addresses and identity
.TP
fleetring\-context\-use(1)
Makes a context current
.TP
fleetring\-context\-remove(1)
Removes a context, but never the files it names
